# File Handling

## What is File Handling?

File handling is used to store and retrieve data from files instead of using the console.

C++ provides the `<fstream>` library for file operations.

---

## File Streams

| Class | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `ifstream` | Read from a file |
| `ofstream` | Write to a file |
| `fstream` | Read and write a file |

---

## Writing to a File

```cpp
#include <fstream>

ofstream file("data.txt");
file << "Hello World";
file.close();
```

---

## Reading from a File

```cpp
#include <fstream>

ifstream file("data.txt");
string text;

file >> text;
cout << text;

file.close();
```

---

## Appending to a File

```cpp
ofstream file("data.txt", ios::app);
file << " Welcome";
file.close();
```

---

## Closing a File

Always close the file after completing file operations.

```cpp
file.close();
```

---

## Important Points

- Include the `<fstream>` header file.
- Use `ofstream` to write to a file.
- Use `ifstream` to read from a file.
- Use `fstream` for both reading and writing.
- Always close the file using `close()`.
